// What each of the 339 spells of the System Reference Document 5.2.1 (CC BY 4.0) does in
// this game. Level, school, range, casting time, class lists and damage dice come from
// shared/srd/spells.json (written by scripts/srd/import-spells.mjs); this table adds the
// icon, the German name, how the engine runs the spell, and a short text in our own words.
//
// The spec is a list of words, read by shared/spells.ts:
//   atk                 spell attack roll            sv:dex      saving throw of the target
//   nosave              it simply happens            auto        damage without a roll
//   dmg                 damage dice from the SRD     d:8d6/1d6   own dice / more per slot level
//   ty:fire             damage type (best = the one the target resists least)
//   half                half damage on a save        rng:60      range in feet, when the SRD says "self"
//   r:20                every enemy this close to the target      n:3/1   targets / more per slot level
//   rays:3/1            attack rolls / more per level             plus    adds the casting modifier
//   c:paralyzed:rep     condition on a failure: a number = turns, rep = save again every turn, hurt = ends on damage
//   zone:20  aura:15    the area stays where it was cast / around the caster and strikes again every turn
//   sus  sus:bonus      free to use again each turn while it lasts (as a bonus action)
//   heal:2d8/2d8        healing / more per level     buff:bless  an effect of SPELL_BUFFS
//   cure:a,b            lifts conditions             revive:1    brings back the dead with that many HP
//   react:shield        cast by itself as a reaction smite       bonus action after a melee hit
//   weapon              one weapon attack            step:30     a jump that provokes no opportunity attacks
//   only:humanoid       creature types it works on   story       the Dungeon Master tells what it does
//   act  bonus  conc  noconc  self  ally  party      corrections to what the SRD data says

